# Quantitative propagation from a seeded horizontal measure (clean inverse-seed spine)

Theorem statement: `HorizontalPadicL.SeededHorizontalPadicLFunctionV4.primePower_propagation_v2`
(`2cfa7bd2-46d8-4152-b8c2-1bc6e45c7c4d`), by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25.

Proof: submission `06cb1ee8-01c9-485a-9fdd-79b601ee48e3`, by davidloeffler, 2026-09-25 (ACCEPTED);
locally adapted.

A seeded horizontal p-adic L-function at an odd prime, whose orderly-prime exponent is a positive
integer m and whose trivial value is nonzero, yields a positive logarithmic-power lower bound for
nonvanishing twists by primitive characters of exact order p^m.

This is the clean-spine replacement used to remove deprecated definition bundles from the live
graph.

## Explanation of the source proof

The uniform integrality of the measure and the lower bound on every local exponent give a finite
Fourier correction outside a fixed finite set. Interpolation and faithful character realization turn
this into a bounded-fibre transfer from supported horizontal characters to primitive Dirichlet
twists. Positive density of the orderly primes supplies a logarithmic-power lower bound for the
source characters; finiteness of bounded-conductor primitive characters and the bounded-fibre
transfer carry the same type of lower bound to the desired twist-counting function.

